      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Logging Providers**\n\nI'm currently evaluating logging providers for this Python script, such as Google Cloud Logging and AWS CloudWatch. The key focus is choosing a managed service to ensure efficient and reliable logging of application events that share a common request identifier.\n\n\n**Selecting Logging Provider Details**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud Logging as the managed logging service. My next step involves creating the `write_correlated_logs.py` file, and implementing a function to handle log messages, correlation IDs, and any other required data. The Google Cloud Logging client library will be used to write structured log entries, ensuring the service is clearly identifiable within the code.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818943381,
          "start": 1789818940885
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b985add5001V6lTvo17m6Vn47",
